-- title:
--   Tube equation for the inertial displacement on an annulus
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\alpha,\beta$ at level $1$ and index $q$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a level-one prolongation pair $R$ for $P$, so that in particular $R$ carries two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F:=\overline{\mathbb Q}\otimes$-base change $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot q)$ with residue maps into $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$. Assume $\mathrm{red}\,c=0$ exactly for $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $a\in k$, let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb Q$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, and let $An$ be an annulus of $F$ along $A$, with parameter $Z=An.\mathrm{param}$ and modulus $\varpi=An.\mathrm{modulus}\in\mathfrak m_A$, such that: the domain of $An$ consists exactly of those places $W$ for which $W.\mathrm{ord}(j-x)>0$ for some $x\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x=a$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q-y)>0$ for some $y\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,y=a^q$ (here $j$ and $j_q$ denote the coefficientwise images of $jq$ and of $\mathtt{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,(1\cdot q)\,jq$); $\varpi\neq0$; the arithmetic Galois action of $\sigma$ fixes $Z$; $\varpi^{-1}Z$ and the Fricke involute of $Z$ both lie, as Laurent series, in the localisation of the ring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $\mathtt{jqModC}$ and $\mathtt{jqNModC}$ at the prime ideal of elements killed by $\mathrm{red}$; and the localised reduction of that Fricke involute is nonzero. Then for every place $V$ of $F$ satisfying the same centring condition as the places of the domain, there exist $x\in A$, a unit $u$ of $A$ and $t\in F$ lying in the valuation rings of both $R_1$ and $R_2$ such that $x\in\mathfrak m_A$, $\varpi=xd$ for some $d\in\mathfrak m_A$, $\sigma(x)=ux$, $Z$ lies in the valuation ring of $V$ with residue the image of $x$, $t=(Z-\sigma(x))(Z-x)^{-1}$, the value of $R.\mathrm{residue}_1$ at $t$ is the image of $\mathrm{red}\,u$ in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, the value of $R.\mathrm{residue}_2$ at $t$ is $1$, and $W.\mathrm{ord}\,t$ equals the coefficient at $W$ of the divisor $\sigma\cdot V-V$ for every place $W$ satisfying that centring condition.
--
--   This is the annulus-level computation of the divisor and of the two residues of the "tube equation" $(Z-\sigma(x))/(Z-x)$ measuring the displacement by inertia of a point $x$ on a tube over a crossing point $(a,a^q)$ of the special fibre of $X_0(q)$, the parameter of the annulus being left abstract rather than given by an explicit coordinate. It feeds the construction of good representatives for divisor classes and the attachment of annuli to component charts of a model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_LevelOneProlongationPair_exists_tubeEquation_smul_sub_self_of_annulus.lean

